quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  21,58,Then he broke them all into pieces—except the biggest of them—so they might return to it.
  21,59,"They said: ‘Who has done this to our gods? Surely, he is among the wrongdoers.’"
  21,60,Some people said: ‘We heard a young man talking about them. He is called Ibrahim (Abraham).’
  21,61,They said: ‘Bring him before the eyes of the people so that they may bear witness (against him).’
  21,62,"They said: ‘Was it you who did this to our gods, O Ibrahim (Abraham)?’"
  21,63,"He said: ‘Surely, this one—the chief of them—has done it. So ask them (i.e. the broken idols) if they can speak.’"
  21,64,"Then they turned to themselves and said (to one another): ‘Indeed, it is you who are the wrongdoers.’"
  21,65,"Then they were made to hang their heads (in shame). They said, ‘You certainly know that they cannot speak.’"
  21,66,"He said: ‘Do you then worship something besides Allah, which can neither benefit you nor harm you?"
  21,67,Shame on you and on what you worship besides Allah! Do you not yet understand?’
  21,68,They said: ‘Burn him and help your gods if you are to take action!’
  21,69,"We said: ‘O fire, be (comfortingly) cool and safe for Ibrahim (Abraham)!’"
  21,70,"They had intended an evil plot against him, but We made them the biggest losers."
  21,71,And We rescued him and Lut* towards the land We had blessed for all nations.
  21,72,"And We gave him (i.e. Abraham) Ishaq (Isaac), and Ya‘qub (Jacob) as an added gift, and each of them We made righteous."
